    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": "United States v. Andre Ralph Hayden was argued before the Supreme Court on February 26, 2019. The dispute centers on whether a district judge may revoke supervised release under 18\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f3583(e)(3) based on a finding of child\u2011pornography possession by a preponderance of the evidence, and whether the same factual finding can support revocation under \u00a7\u202f3583(k). The United States argues that the preponderance finding is sufficient for both statutes, while the respondent contends that \u00a7\u202f3583(k) stretches the original jury\u2011authorized sentence and imposes additional imprisonment only under limited circumstances.",
    "summary_citations": [
      {
        "document_hash": "fa2afda9ecdd54f12884b7a045852688847a0464138a95fcfd2f3945949e18c4",
        "evidence_ids": [
