              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Eric J. Feigin, the district judge's finding by a preponderance of the evidence is constitutionally sufficient to revoke supervised release under \u00a7\u202f3583(e)(3)."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "fa2afda9ecdd54f12884b7a045852688847a0464138a95fcfd2f3945949e18c4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-fa2afda9ecdd-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Feigin, the Sixth Amendment does not apply, so Apprendi does not apply in this context."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "fa2afda9ecdd54f12884b7a045852688847a0464138a95fcfd2f3945949e18c4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-fa2afda9ecdd-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Feigin, the jury's verdict authorizes revocation under \u00a7\u202f3583(k) just as it does under \u00a7\u202f3583(e)(3)."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "United States (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Lunn",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "fa2afda9ecdd54f12884b7a045852688847a0464138a95fcfd2f3945949e18c4",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-fa2afda9ecdd-0001-0004"
